Z||000004||151 in. of love||02-10-2001||12:52 PM||||That reminds me of the Magnasteer function on the Grand Prix (99 or 00). Anyone familiar with that?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||02-10-2001||07:58 PM||||Yup. I've got Magnasteer on my 99 Grand Am.  It's a good feeling power steering.  On my Fiero, though, I don't think I'd want power steering.  The effort isn't too bad, and you get much better road feel than with any type of power steering.<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||02-11-2001||11:37 AM||||What exactly is magnasteer?||||reg||1
Z||000007||151 in. of love||02-11-2001||05:24 PM||||Based on the very little knowledge I have of this component. I think that I have somewhat of an idea.<P>It is supplemental to the power steering function as I understand.<P>It is a magnetic coil that wraps around the rack. It is speed sensitive and increases the voltage to the coil accordingly. Adding resistance to the steering with the increase of speed. The function is based on the idea of the standard speed sensitive steering through orifices. (I believe) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyone else?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||02-12-2001||10:34 PM||||I was thinking that an integrated motor-pump like that would be great to use a a pre-oiler to extend engine life.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||02-12-2001||11:43 PM||||The great things GM doesn't do...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>If your 88 was built late enough in the production run, your steering rack probably has the hookups for the power steering pump.||||reg||1
